WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:01.010
The Division Crosses the Sea

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.280
You're clear. Keep it coming.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.960
That's Division 2;
the ones that are so aggressive.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.540
They don't guard the
capitol, they wreck it!

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:37.590
They're scary!

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.180
We're safe, as long as they stay put.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.390
Why'd they bring
those dangerous things here?!

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.390
It's facing this way.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.320
I'd like to warm up both units.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.940
Shige and the crew were worried
about cold-weather operation.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:02.200
The Labors weren't
designed for this cold.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.070
Don't sweat it.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:07.240
The other Labors
all seem to be doing fine.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.370
I'm going
to the provisional headquarters.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.470
A publicity stunt?

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.300
We're "volunteers," but it's all
just a publicity stunt.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:30.060
It's not the life or death situation we are
trained for, but it makes a difference.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.100
Helping the Sapporo Winter
Festival improves our image...

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.560
and by extension,
the image of the entire force.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.780
This'll earn us some
brownie points, that's for sure.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:39.780
I dunno.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:40.530
What?

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.610
It doesn't really make sense.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:47.120
They wouldn't leave Division 1
as the capitol's only defense.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.200
Maybe there's more to it.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.880
You with the Labor team?

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.000
How about lending a hand?

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.840
Your friend thinks he deserves a break.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.640
Making a couple of these is a snap, Izumi!

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.900
He gets off on the strangest things.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.570
Hey, you aren't bad, little lady.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.860
Dump the police and work for me!

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.910
I hear you're from around here.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.160
Moving back would make
your old man happy.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.930
...walking in a winter wonderland!

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:52.930
Ota!

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.410
Hey, phone call for you.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.160
A phone call?

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.330
I've been wondering how it's going.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.380
Great, if you don't like excitement.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:20.380
I feel like a junior high chaperone.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.800
You always look on the bright side.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:25.550
Don't frown, you'll get wrinkles.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.930
So, jokes aside,
have you learned anything?

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:32.510
Like why we were actually
sent to Hokkaido?

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:38.770
You know as well as I do that the Earth
Defense Army hates the Babylon Project.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:44.490
Captain Goto, the rebel factions
have just released a threat.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:45.440
Really?

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:47.650
They've targeted the Winter Festival.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:50.780
The news isn't being released
to the public.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.950
But apparently two Hishii Labors...

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.370
have been stolen from the shop
while they were in for repairs.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.250
That's trouble.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:02.250
What caught my attention
was the part that said, "Beware of L."

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.590
The Earth Defense Army
specializes in Labor crime.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.300
I wonder if they meant,
"Beware of Labors?"

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.890
The threat was written
on a computer...

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:15.430
and sent to the police,
the papers, and TV stations.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.100
Listen, Shinobu.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.850
What if this threat against
the Winter Festival is a fake-out...

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:23.940
and the capitol is
in fact their real target?

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.780
Don't worry.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.740
That's why the section chief
left Division 1 behind.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.370
The Labor Team!

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:32.280
They're here!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:33.580
Cool!

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.910
Don't run or you'll slip!

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.260
I'm glad we brought Hiromi.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.680
He looks so bored
everyone felt sorry for us.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.470
A victory for personnel.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.050
Anyway, they say they
don't want any more help.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.430
I'm sure.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:58.890
This was Izumi's fault!
If she hadn't butted in...!

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:01.350
You think I'm to blame, Ota?

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:05.150
I'd just like to know
where the creep is...

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.360
who threw those sheets
underneath my Labor?

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:12.610
He's the guy to pin it on!
Why didn't you catch him?

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.490
We couldn't. We were too
busy picking up after you.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.960
We're trapped in
a frozen wasteland...

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.830
while the people around us
play like demented children.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:29.050
You Japanese people like
the strangest things.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:30.880
It's a Patlabor!

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:32.380
It's huge!

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:33.640
Holy cow dude!

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.050
There's two of them!

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.770
Model AV-98 "Ingram," manufactured
by Shinohara Heavy Industries.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.190
Height: 8.02 meters.
Width: 4.37 meters.

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.900
Weight: 6.02 tons.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:49.360
Turning radius: 3.9 meters.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:54.160
Standard issue: 37mm,
6-shot revolver cannon.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:59.580
Lightweight, agile,
and highly dexterous.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.330
It is the finest Labor in
use by any police force.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:06.380
Oh, that's right!

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.210
Satoru you just came from Tokyo.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.720
They have lots
of construction Labors there...

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.050
that are also working
on the Babylon Project.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.430
But Satoru said he hates Labors!

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:20.310
Then he shouldn't have
come to see them!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:21.390
What a weirdo!

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.810
Weirdo! Weirdo!

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.900
Satoru, put that down!

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:32.780
Look, Izumi!

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.150
There's Babylon Castle!

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:41.700
The Babylon Development
Corporation is sponsoring it.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.830
It's the showpiece of the festival.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.330
Come back here!

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.560
Satoru!

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:03.930
Who threw that snowball at Alphonse?

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:05.520
You idiot!

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:06.900
Hiromi!

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.320
Sorry about that, Hiromi.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.530
That's all right.

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:16.950
Noa, is that you?

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.660
Kiyama, unreal!

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:25.120
You were on Noa's basketball
team in high school?

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:30.090
I really can't believe you're doing your
student teaching here in Sapporo.

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:31.800
I'm the shocked one.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.880
I knew you were a cop in Tokyo...

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.630
and I'd heard you'd
joined Special Vehicles.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:40.550
But I didn't know you were
with the infamous Patlabor Div. 2!

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.600
Sounds like disasters follow you.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:45.480
Disasters?

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:51.110
We've heard of Division 2's
"mishaps," even way up here!

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.940
Is it true you got tangled up
in a broadcast tower?

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:55.780
Yeah...

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.780
One of the boys in my class
just moved here from Tokyo...

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.070
and has been through a lot.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:05.660
A Patlabor totaled his house so he
was forced to move to Hokkaido.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.620
The boy hanging out earlier?

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:10.290
Yeah, his name's Satoru.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.840
I think he used to love Labors
before he moved up here.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.510
But he can't stand them,
since they demolished his house.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.590
My heart goes out to the poor kid.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.970
He despises them.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:22.970
What a sad story.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:27.480
I'm sure it was just an accident.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:30.440
Sometimes these things
can't be helped!

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:32.730
Are you sure about that?

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:47.580
So the festival
really is their target.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:53.790
Captain Nagumo was right.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:56.380
That's one of the stolen Hishii Labors.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:59.380
First they set a time bomb,
then abandoned it.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:02.840
A new threat has just
arrived at the Provisional HQ.

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:03.640
Another one?

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:07.350
"We'll smash your Babylon
Project with an iron hammer."

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:08.770
The same MO.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:10.980
It's like they have
a manual or something.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.610
"Slogans for the Revolution,"
"Terminology for Terrorists"...

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:18.240
"How to Incite a War," and
"You Too Can Write a Manifesto."

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.200
Anarchist scum!

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:27.160
Perhaps the terrorists will still try to
carry out something during the festival.

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:28.370
Could be.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.540
They only have one Labor left.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:34.130
They just don't strike me
as the types to let it sit around idly.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:38.090
Those sheets I slipped on were
probably terrorist work too!

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.880
They WANTED me to
crush that snow sculpture!

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.590
I doubt it.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:45.100
- Why?!
- Just a hunch, that's all!

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.060
"Just a hunch" is no reason!

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:49.470
Hiromi, come here a second.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.060
Do this. That's right.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.070
Hey, let me go Yamazaki!

00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:59.900
Come on let's go, Kiyama.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:01.610
Yamazaki!

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.490
How long do you think
I should keep this up?

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.070
Let go!

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:05.070
Who knows?

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:10.580
Satoru threw a slippery, plastic sheet
under a Labor's feet?

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.750
Uh-huh, I figured you knew
something about it.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.000
Asuma!

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.880
The offense and defense
are one heart, one mind.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.170
I had a right to eavesdrop.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.840
Do you really think that
kid hates us so much?

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:25.180
I just don't want to believe it.

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:28.220
He used to love Labors,
but now he can't stand them.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:31.930
When you're betrayed
by the one you love, you do a 180.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.940
Even an adult would have
a complete change of feelings.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:40.440
Noa, let me find
Satoru and talk to him myself.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.190
Don't tell anyone about
this until then, okay?

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:45.320
Okay.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.410
I won't tell anyone.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.680
Pickle

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:37.580
It's freezing.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:42.460
Noa...

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.410
It isn't your fault, Alphonse.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.530
I won't let anyone pin it on you.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.540
You work so hard.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:40.210
Noa, where are you?

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.000
Here!

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:41.620
Catch!

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:44.790
The system disk?
Did something happen?

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:45.750
I'm not sure.

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:49.550
I saw a Labor doing something
at the west side of the park.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:50.920
Check it out!

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:51.680
Roger!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.310
We're off! Outta the way!

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:12.030
Attention: Halt your Labor
and exit the cockpit immediately!

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:20.160
Stop it, I said!

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:24.750
You creep!

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.670
What are you doing?
Fight back!

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:31.670
Easy for you to say!

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:33.720
You have the upper hand!

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.600
I don't want to smash the sculptures.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.100
Get up, Noa!

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:51.070
Chew on this!

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.240
Stop it, Ota!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.870
You'll destroy the sculptures!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.370
Stay out of this, Izumi!

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:02.540
Outta here!

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:13.630
Hello.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.380
Welcome aboard.

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:21.640
The would-be terrorists were eager
to brag about their scheme.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:26.440
They've planted a bomb
that will go off at noon.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:27.850
What?!

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:31.360
Izumi, Ota, check out
the snow sculptures.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:33.820
The bomb should be
inside one of them.

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:38.820
Shinshi, go to the tent and act
as relay for the command cars.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:42.580
Everyone else help Izumi and Ota
search for the bomb.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:43.700
Roger.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:52.250
There're too many to search.
We'll never find it!

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:55.420
Why don't you look for Labor
footprints in the snow.

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:58.470
You chased him so much last night,
the whole place is trampled.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.220
Listen up. We've got to do something.

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:04.770
The crowd will start arriving after 11.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:07.020
Less than two hours left!

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.390
Do what you can.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.650
What if we don't find it?

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:11.650
Ka-boom.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.290
Think we'll ever find it?

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:35.510
Less talking, more looking!

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:38.470
We're just running around like
chickens with our heads cut off.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.930
Noa, think like a criminal.

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:46.350
Where would you bury a bomb
if you were using a Labor?

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:49.190
Most of these sculptures are
too heavy to lift...

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.900
and would break if I even tried.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:54.860
So, I'd pull out a block and
hide the bomb behind it!

00:18:55.400 --> 00:19:00.320
But that would leave marks
where I grabbed the block!

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:00.990
Right!

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.410
Check for marks!

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:04.330
But that'd be hard...

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.160
There's no time for whining!

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:08.000
All right.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:11.080
Excuse me.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:12.460
I need to talk to Noa
about this boy.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:16.050
Izumi? Afraid she's tied up right now.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:19.920
She's got her hands full,
searching for a bomb.

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.010
What? A bomb?

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:24.220
You sent a woman
on such a dangerous mission?

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.600
Why not? That's her job.

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:27.850
Still...

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:39.610
Why don't we just smash the sculptures.
Wouldn't that be the easiest way?

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.990
Looking for a bomb in that
mess would be even harder.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.870
We definitely shouldn't smash them!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.080
We have to find the bomb another way!

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:01.050
Goto, it's no use!

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:02.380
We can't find it!

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:04.470
You have to find it!

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.550
Although that's easier said than done.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:08.390
Hold it...

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:13.650
Babylon Castle... Babylon Project...
Babylon...

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:16.610
That's it!

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:26.620
It's in the Babylon Castle!
Search the blocks in the letter "L"!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:29.620
Satoru, where are you going?

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:30.700
Get outta there!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.120
Satoru!

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:34.750
No, let me go!

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:38.420
Look!

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:40.050
There it is!

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.020
Slowly now, take your time.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:20:59.650
Found it!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:01.820
Noa!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:06.240
What's wrong, Noa?

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:08.450
I can't get it, the hole's too small.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:10.120
Use the feedback gloves.

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:12.200
All right, I'll try.

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:20.920
Be careful.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:37.730
Got it!

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:40.980
Throw it as high as you can!

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:44.440
Ota!

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:45.820
Piece of cake!

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.170
Oh, Shinobu!

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:02.090
Oh, Captain Goto,
I'm glad you're safe.

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:05.670
You know, it's a good thing
they only used one bomb.

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:06.550
Huh?

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:08.630
Oh, yes, I suppose.

00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:11.760
Terrorists sometimes plant others,
don't they?

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:14.270
Luckily, not this time.

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:16.350
The festival is beautiful.
I wish you could see it.

00:22:16.680 --> 00:22:19.150
I can.
I'm watching it right now.

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:20.770
What? How?

00:22:42.630 --> 00:22:45.840
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:49.550
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:55.810
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:05.320
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:08.240
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:12.820
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:17.500
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:20.330
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:24.500
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:31.010
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:36.260
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:38.810
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:42.020
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:46.110
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:52.280
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:58.330
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:04.960
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:10.050
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:10.050
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:17.600
Captain Goto used to be
as sharp as a tack. What happened?

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:21.310
After 20 years with Special Vehicles 2nd
Section his past remains a mystery.

00:24:21.310 --> 00:24:23.190
Could some sort of
unknown incident from his past...

00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:24.980
Have changed the
direction of his life?

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:27.900
Captain Goto is quite an enigma.

00:24:28.110 --> 00:24:29.530
Nobody even knows
who this guy REALLY is.

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:32.240
I really want to know!!

00:24:32.700 --> 00:24:35.410
Next episode:
"Target: Captain Goto."

00:24:35.780 --> 00:24:37.660
Target locked on!

00:24:36.950 --> 00:24:41.950
Next episode

